file: manage a file

At most one of content, template, source, copy_from, and stock sets the
content. A step without any of them manages only the owner, group, and
mode that it gives, of a file that exists. The step creates missing
parent directories, owned by root with mode 0755.

Keys:
  path       string      required  absolute
  content    string      -         literal text
  template   string      -         file in the recipe's templates/
  source     string      -         file in the recipe's files/
  copy_from  string      -         file on the host
  stock      boolean     false     content that the package ships
  owner      name or ID  root
  group      name or ID  root
  mode       string      0644      octal, in quotes
  validate   string      -         check command for the new file
  absent     boolean     false
  replace    boolean     false     remove another kind of thing at path first

Example:
  - name: Write the message of the day
    file:
      path: /etc/motd
      content: "Welcome to mail.example.com.\n"
      mode: "0644"

Run "winch doc file.<key>" for the full text of a key.
